<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n31194" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Nōra</span></b> , ōrum,
		n., = <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">Νῶρα</span>. <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b>
			<i>A hill-fort between Lycaonia and Cappadocia</i>,
				<i><span class="en">Nep.
				Eum. 5, 3</span></i>.—</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>II.</b>
			<i>A very ancient city in Sardinia</i>, now <i>Nori</i>.—Hence, </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>B.</b>
			<b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Nōrensis</span></b> ,
			e, <i>adj., of</i> or <i>belonging to Nora</i>, <i><span class="en">Cic. Scaur. 1, 4</span></i>, c.—In
				plur.: <b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Nōrenses</span></b> , ĭum,
				m., <i>the inhabitants of Nora</i>,
				<i><span class="en">Cic.
				Scaur. 2, 9</span></i>; <i><span class="en">Plin. 3, 7, 13, §
			85</span></i>.—</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>III.</b>
			<i>A city of India</i>, <i><span class="en">Curt. 8,
				11, 1</span></i>; v. Mütz, ad h. l.</div>
    </div> <div class="alpheios-lex-footnotes en"> </div>
